---
// BlastRadius case study: problem -> decision -> what it does -> measured result -> install.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ArchDiagram from '../../components/ArchDiagram.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
import blastradius from '../../data/diagrams/blastradius.json';

const description =
  'BlastRadius gives Claude Code memory across repository boundaries. It indexes Docker images, Terraform modules, GitHub Actions, Helm charts and npm packages, warns which other repos an artifact reaches before you change it, and filters CVEs down to the ones your pins actually resolve to.';

const repo = 'https://github.com/harris-ahmad/blastradius-mcp';
const pypi = 'https://pypi.org/project/blastradius-mcp/';

const schema = [
  {
    '@type': 'SoftwareSourceCode',
    '@id': `${site.url}/blastradius/#software`,
    name: 'BlastRadius',
    description,
    url: `${site.url}/blastradius/`,
    codeRepository: repo,
    programmingLanguage: 'Python',
    license: 'https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT',
    author: { '@id': `${site.url}/#person` },
  },
];
---
<Base
  title="BlastRadius — cross-repo infrastructure memory for coding agents"
  description={description}
  path="/blastradius/"
  nav="projects"
  schema={schema}
>
  <header class="page-head hero">
    <p class="kicker">Open source · MIT</p>
    <h1>BlastRadius</h1>
    <p class="lede">Cross-repo infrastructure memory for coding agents. It knows who else depends on an artifact <em>before</em> you change it, and watches those pins for vulnerabilities while nobody is asking.</p>
    <p class="result"><span class="tag">Result</span><span>39/39 artifacts found · 39/39 version specs intact · 0 false positives</span><span class="ctx">planted 6-repo corpus</span></p>
    <p class="well install"><span class="c prompt" aria-hidden="true">$ </span><code>pip install blastradius-mcp</code></p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn" href={repo}>GitHub</a>
      <a href={pypi}>PyPI</a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="case">
    <!-- 01 Problem -->
    <section class="hang sec" aria-labelledby="problem">
      <div class="m"><span class="n">01</span><span>problem</span></div>
      <div class="body">
        <h2 id="problem">The problem</h2>
        <p>A coding agent is excellent inside one repository and blind across many. Bump a base image, retag a GitHub Action, move a Terraform module — nothing tells you the four other repositories pinning the same thing. The knowledge exists. It just isn’t anywhere the agent will look.</p>
        <p>This is not a code graph. Excellent tools already index functions, classes and imports. BlastRadius indexes the other half — the infrastructure artifacts — and answers the question a single session cannot: <strong>if I bump this, who breaks?</strong></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 02 Decision -->
    <section class="hang sec" aria-labelledby="decision">
      <div class="m"><span class="n">02</span><span>decision</span></div>
      <div class="body">
        <h2 id="decision">The idea: hooks, not tools</h2>
        <p>An MCP server can expose a perfect tool and the model can simply not call it. Nothing errors, nothing is misconfigured — the information just doesn’t arrive, and you cannot tell “no impact found” from “never asked.”</p>
        <p>Hooks invert that. The harness runs them, so what they return lands in context whether the model wanted it or not. That single distinction decided the architecture.</p>

        <ol class="flow" aria-label="The two hooks">
          <li>
            <span class="node">Agent reads <code>package.json</code></span>
            <span class="to"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="visually-hidden">then</span></span>
            <span class="node hook"><code class="hk">PreToolUse</code><span>inject</span></span>
            <span class="to"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="visually-hidden">then</span></span>
            <span class="node out">Cross-repo impact, unprompted</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="node">Session ends</span>
            <span class="to"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="visually-hidden">then</span></span>
            <span class="node hook"><code class="hk">Stop</code><span>capture</span></span>
            <span class="to"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="visually-hidden">then</span></span>
            <span class="node out">Index learns this repo</span>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <div class="hang note">
          <div class="m label">Tradeoff</div>
          <p>The tradeoff is real: you spend context on every matching tool call, deterministically. So the cost is measured rather than assumed — <code>blastradius cost</code> reports what every injection spends — and it stays silent unless something is genuinely shared.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Architecture as of blastradius-mcp v0.3.2 -->
        <figure class="arch" id="architecture">
          <ArchDiagram id="br-case" data={blastradius as any} label="BlastRadius architecture diagram" />
          <figcaption><span class="strong">Architecture</span> — When the agent reads, edits or runs a command on a manifest, a PreToolUse hook looks up the local SQLite index and injects which other repos depend on that artifact and how tightly each pins it (blue path). At Stop, a second hook lists manifests the index hasn’t seen, and the agent records them through the MCP server, which reads exact versions from lockfiles. Outside the session (dashed), a launchd/systemd watcher syncs OSV advisories into the same index and can post new ones to Slack.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 03 What it does unasked -->
    <section class="hang sec" aria-labelledby="unasked">
      <div class="m"><span class="n">03</span><span>in practice</span></div>
      <div class="body">
        <h2 id="unasked">What it does unasked</h2>
        <p>Open a repo, ask for something ordinary — <em>“bump react to 19”</em> — and before the agent reads a line of <code>package.json</code>, a hook has already told it:</p>
        <blockquote class="said">
          <p><code>acme/checkout</code> (a separate repo) also depends on <code>react@^18.2.0</code>, and <code>lodash</code> here is shared with <code>acme/notifications</code> and <code>acme/checkout</code> too.</p>
        </blockquote>
        <p>Two repositories that were not open, not mentioned, and have no trace in the working directory. The agent never called a tool to find them.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 04 What it produces -->
    <section class="hang sec" aria-labelledby="output">
      <div class="m"><span class="n">04</span><span>output</span></div>
      <div class="body">
        <h2 id="output">And what it produces</h2>
        <ul class="funnel" aria-label="Advisory filtering">
          <li><span class="big">43</span><span class="what">advisories from OSV</span></li>
          <li><span class="big">9</span><span class="what">that apply to your pinned versions</span></li>
        </ul>

        <pre class="well term" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Sample BlastRadius vulnerability report (scrolls sideways on small screens)"><code><span class="sev crit">[CRITICAL]</span> vitest                 CVE-2026-47429
           When Vitest UI server is listening, arbitrary file
           can be read and executed
           <span class="c">reaches:</span> 3.2.4  (installed version)
           <span class="c">in:</span>      acme/checkout
<span class="sev high">[HIGH    ]</span> lodash                 CVE-2021-23337
           lodash vulnerable to Code Injection via `_.template`
           <span class="c">reaches:</span> 4.17.21, ^4.17.21</code></pre>

        <p>Advisories are matched against what your pins can <em>actually resolve to</em>. A manifest saying <code>^5.2.0</code> permits a vulnerable 5.2.0; the lockfile saying <code>5.4.19</code> permits none of them. For <code>vite</code> alone that is the difference between 13 alerts and 6. Anything unknowable — a floating tag, a digest, a git ref — stays flagged, because hiding a real vulnerability is far worse than showing one that turns out not to apply.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 05 Measured result -->
    <section class="hang sec" aria-labelledby="measured">
      <div class="m"><span class="n">05</span><span>result</span></div>
      <div class="body">
        <h2 id="measured">Measured, not asserted</h2>
        <p>Extraction is scored against a planted corpus of six repositories with <strong>the hard cases put there on purpose</strong>: multi-stage build aliases, <code>ARG</code>-templated base images, a <code>FROM</code> inside a heredoc, relative module sources, <code>workspace:</code> protocols, and a registry with a port that looks like a tag.</p>

        <ul class="stats" aria-label="Extraction results">
          <li><span class="big">39/39</span><span class="what">artifacts found</span></li>
          <li class="key"><span class="big">39/39</span><span class="what">version specs intact</span></li>
          <li><span class="big">0</span><span class="what">false positives</span></li>
          <li><span class="big">6</span><span class="what">planted repositories</span></li>
        </ul>

        <div class="hang note">
          <div class="m label">Note</div>
          <p><strong>The second number is the one that matters.</strong> A model that quietly normalises <code>^18.2.0</code> to <code>18.2.0</code> scores full recall while destroying the entire signal — the range operator is the information. Recall alone would report 100% on output that is worthless.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 06 Install -->
    <section class="hang sec" aria-labelledby="install">
      <div class="m"><span class="n">06</span><span>install</span></div>
      <div class="body">
        <h2 id="install">Install</h2>
        <p>Everything is local: one SQLite file at <code>~/.blastradius/index.db</code>. No account, no server, no API key, nothing leaves your machine.</p>

        <pre class="well term" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Install commands (scrolls sideways on small screens)"><code>pip install blastradius-mcp

blastradius install     <span class="c"># wire hooks + MCP server into Claude Code</span>
blastradius doctor      <span class="c"># verify — by running the hooks for real</span>
blastradius index ~/code  <span class="c"># bootstrap from repos you already have</span></code></pre>

        <p>Or as a Claude Code plugin:</p>

        <pre class="well term" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Claude Code plugin commands (scrolls sideways on small screens)"><code>/plugin marketplace add harris-ahmad/blastradius-mcp
/plugin install blastradius@blastradius</code></pre>

        <div class="hang note">
          <div class="m label">Bootstrap</div>
          <p>That last bootstrap step matters more than it looks. Capture runs when a session ends — <em>after</em> the reads — and cross-repo impact needs a second indexed repository before it has anything to say. Without it the tool is correct and completely silent for days.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Closing -->
    <div class="hang sec closing">
      <div class="m label">Source</div>
      <div class="body">
        <p>376 tests across 3.6K lines in 16 modules, run on Python 3.11–3.13. MIT licensed.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="btn" href={repo}>Read the source</a>
          <a href={pypi}>blastradius-mcp on PyPI</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .strong {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  /* Hero (doubled class so these win over .page-head whatever the stylesheet order) */
  .page-head.hero {
    gap: 1.125rem;
  }

  .page-head.hero h1 {
    font-size: 3rem;
    line-height: 1.02;
  }

  .page-head.hero .lede {
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  .result {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: .125rem .75rem;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: .8125rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .result .ctx {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .result .tag {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: .75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: .12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  .install {
    display: block;
    width: fit-content;
    max-width: 100%;
    margin-top: .375rem;
    font-size: .875rem;
  }

  .install code {
    font-size: inherit;
  }

  .prompt {
    user-select: none;
  }

  .actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: .5rem 1.75rem;
  }

  .actions > a:not(.btn) {
    min-height: 2.75rem;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    font-size: .9375rem;
  }

  /* Case study sections */
  .case {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4rem;
  }

  .sec {
    padding-top: 1.75rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .sec > .m {
    line-height: 1.9;
  }

  .body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.125rem;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .body > p {
    max-width: 38rem;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .body h2 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -.01em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .body strong {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* Inline code in running text */
  p code,
  .node code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: .875em;
    padding: .0625rem .3125rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
    background: var(--tint);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .install code {
    padding: 0;
    background: none;
  }

  /* Margin notes inside a section */
  .note {
    margin-top: .375rem;
  }

  .note p {
    max-width: 38rem;
    font-size: .9375rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .note strong {
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  /* Hook flow: event -> hook -> result, one row per hook */
  .flow {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: .75rem;
    margin: .5rem 0;
  }

  .flow > li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto minmax(0, 1fr);
    align-items: stretch;
    gap: .625rem;
  }

  .node {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: .125rem;
    min-height: 3.5rem;
    padding: .5rem .75rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-ink);
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: var(--bg);
    font-size: .875rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .node.hook {
    border: 1.5px solid var(--accent);
  }

  .node.hook > span {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .node .hk {
    padding: 0;
    background: none;
    font-size: .8125rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .node.out {
    border-color: var(--rule-strong);
    background: var(--tint);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .to {
    align-self: center;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    color: var(--faint);
  }

  /* Quoted hook output */
  .said {
    max-width: 38rem;
    padding: .25rem 0 .25rem 1.125rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--rule-strong);
  }

  .said p {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .said code {
    font-size: .75em;
  }

  /* Terminal output and commands */
  .term {
    display: block;
    width: fit-content;
    max-width: 100%;
    margin: .25rem 0;
    padding: .875rem 1rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    overflow-wrap: normal;
    white-space: pre;
  }

  .sev {
    margin: 0 -.25rem;
    padding: 0 .25rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .sev.crit {
    background: var(--fg);
    color: var(--well);
  }

  .sev.high {
    background: var(--well-line);
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  /* Number strips, in the homepage proof-strip style */
  .funnel,
  .stats {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem 2rem;
    padding: 1.25rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .funnel {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(14rem, 100%), 1fr));
  }

  .stats {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(9rem, 100%), 1fr));
    margin: .5rem 0;
  }

  .funnel li,
  .stats li {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: .25rem;
  }

  .big {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -.03em;
  }

  .what {
    font-size: .9375rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .stats .key .big {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .stats .key .what {
    color: var(--fg);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  /* Architecture figure (same treatment as the homepage) */
  .arch {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: .625rem;
    min-width: 0;
    margin-top: .75rem;
  }

  .arch figcaption {
    max-width: 40rem;
    font-size: .875rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  /* Closing */
  .closing .body > p {
    font-size: .9375rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .page-head.hero h1 {
      font-size: 2.25rem;
    }

    .case {
      gap: 3rem;
    }

    .body h2 {
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    .said p {
      font-size: 1.0625rem;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .flow {
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }

    .flow > li {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: .375rem;
    }

    .node {
      min-height: 2.75rem;
    }

    .to {
      justify-self: start;
      padding-left: 1rem;
      transform: rotate(90deg);
    }
  }
</style>
